<title>CANADA: Minister to meet Canadian management, union.</title>
<headline>Minister to meet Canadian management, union.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Transport Minister David Anderson was in Vancouver on Monday to meet with the management and unions of troubled carrier Canadian Airlines Corp, a source at Transport Canada said.</p>
<p>But the source said Ottawa had no immediate plans to bail out the cash-strapped airline, which has said it faced bankruptcy if a tough restructuring plan was not accepted by its unions over the next few days.</p>
<p>&quot;The minister went to Vancouver to act as an observer,&quot; the source said. &quot;The minister did not go with a check.</p>
</text>
